\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\deftab1195\f0\fs24\cf0
\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 A Solitant priest hears the word \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8216\'91white\u8217\'92 and thinks of the pure white glow of Solraheen, a white so bright it bursts out of itself and splits softly into rays of red, green, and blue. Hrkan folk hear \u8216\'91white\u8217\'92 and think of the plain and stainless robes of Hrkan Lordship. Outland pokes hear \u8216\'91white\u8217\'92 and think of sparkling salt pans, or sun-bleached bone. As it is with white, so it is with words, they evoke different meanings in different people. It is some wonder then, that Solraheen would choose to use such an equivocal thing as a word to create the world. He dwelt in the void, spoke one word, the world emerged, and people haven\u8217\'92t stopped arguing about the meaning of it all ever since.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 One might be led to believe that Solraheen chose to create with a word because He wanted to play with what He meant.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93But this is false,\u8221\'94 Vigram said curtly. The big man leaned forward and swiped his belly beard down against his stomach so that he could rest his elbows clean on the dining table. Hands clasped, he struck a thoughtful pose. He stared out at Mandri from beneath his dark, tufted brow for what seemed like an eternity.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Consider,\u8221\'94 he finally said, \u8220\'93when Solraheen walked the earth, an artwork was nothing less than a divine message given physical form. Then evil entered the world, twisted the tongues of men, and now the heresy of art as a means of personal expression pollutes the age. I should include you in this as well; you\u8217\'92re an artist. Artists are degenerates.\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri shrugged, as if to concede the point. He held his tongue because he didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t believe in inflicting his opinions on people he\u8217\'92d just met. Vigram obviously felt differently. The man was absolutely riddled with opinions. And Vigram wasn\u8217\'92t some skinny person with a scholar\u8217\'92s neck, one of those people with a mind so deep that they forget to eat and so you could be sure that they have interesting things to say. Vigram had probably never missed a meal in his life. His jowels sort of flapped while he spoke. And he had a brutish aspect; bald, with a broad face, fiftyish years old, talked with his hands\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 disgusting. These were indelicate gestures, as if he were performing a kind of amateur surgery, amputating uncultured ideas, excising that gangrenous degeneracy by means of interrogation.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 But Mandri had heard it all before. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 What is art?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Who is an artist?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Who isn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 A painter, a sculptor, these are artists, yes, that\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s reasonable to say, but what about a tax collector? Is he an artist too if he plumbs the depths of greed? Is a sheep-shearer plying her shears an artist if she\u8217\'92s sufficiently clever about it? What about a farmer? Give a young man a shovel, a field of dirt, friends to impress, and what does he do? He\u8217\'92ll dig a penis. The average Jandri boy will find it funny to dig a big old ugly in the dirt. He laughs because it doubles as a drainage ditch, just like the real thing. And to place such degeneracy in the same category as the cloud of colored windows which open up the ceiling of the Gambagall\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 well! As Vigram would attest, }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 that}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  is an affront to the sacred.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s unintelligible!\u8221\'94 Vigram declared, a full throated bellow. \u8220\'93If everyone is an artist, then the word is as useful as an unmarked weight!\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I don\u8217\'92t mean to interrupt,\u8221\'94 Mandri said cautiously, \u8220\'93But, maybe we should begin the lesson?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram came down from his cloud and waved Mandri off. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93About that,\u8221\'94 he said. \u8220\'93I should mention that we\u8217\'92re waiting for a third.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93A third? Who?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram inhaled deeply. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93She prefers to introduce herself,\u8221\'94 he said. \u8220\'93She is often busy. She will be here shortly. In the meantime, I\u8217\'92ve some food coming, or I should say, it should already be here.\u8221\'94 He cast an impatient eye towards the kitchen door. Then he pounded his table with his fat hand, and glared at the door until one of his slaves shouted, \u8220\'93Coming!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The door popped open. Out came a slave girl carrying two steaming plates of leech. Then came another, ferrying more incomprehensible plates and bowls of leech. This was Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s leech farm, and so every dish\u8217\'92s principal ingredient was some variation of the Meskalimi leech. This particular leech was a prized delicacy throughout the Hrkan world, as the meat, if it can be called meat, cured infertility, and somehow, fertility as well. It was also quite sweet and chewy. Each bite would force the tongue into acrobatics.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93We\u8217\'92re not in any rush,\u8221\'94 Vigram said as he pulled a bowl of leechy porridge towards his belly. \u8220\'93It will take you a good long while to get comfortable around me. You see, I\u8217\'92m a difficult student. I require a very specific type of instruction. I require a painter who fits me like a glove, as they say. Preferably, someone who understands what this world is coming to. You see, I need to know if you can }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 see}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  the degeneracy, how it eats away at our shared foundations. The Lords are too high up to see it. Art itself\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 the last bastion of sacred feeling\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 when art itself degenerates, then you know that a people have lost the principles which bind them together. I tell you, a great an chaos is coming for us.\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram stabbed his spoon into his porridge, took a bite, then continued ranting about how artists were all invalids.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri was careful not to listen. If he listened, he would inevitably say what he really thought, and that would start an argument. It might even get him fired before he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d gotten paid. But he wasn\u8217\'92t good at feigning attention either, not with Vigram bloviating all over the food. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He chowed down on the cold, crumbled chunks of what he supposed was boiled leech. It was quite bitter on account of the overpowering sauce, but the effort to suppress a gag helped keep him from speaking his mind. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He chewed and chewed. Thin strips of sweetened leech slipped around his tongue. Vigram had moved on the subject of inspiration and mathematics. Mandri distracted himself by appreciating the subtleties of the room, none of which could be captured in a painting. The cool, dark grays in the shadowy corners called for a shade of blue which he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d never been able to find, or mix. The blackwood floor creaked under his chair every time he shifted his weight, and that sound, that tactile sense of something old expiring in the humidity, that could only be hinted at in an image. Two windows set into the long wall behind him sent breakfast sunbeams slanting across the sturdy table. That light was alive with dust motes fleeing Vigram\u8217\'92s prattle. Then there was the ceiling, which sagged and cracked, as though the plastered clay had given up. The sense of dread that sag elicited could only be felt if one was sitting underneath it and looking up.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You don\u8217\'92t agree?\u8221\'94 Vigram asked.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Oh, no, I was just thinking,\u8221\'94 Mandri said.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93About what?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I guess I was wondering, why not choose a different word?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93A different word for what?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Art. If people have corrupted the word, you could maybe make a new one.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram soured. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Words must have walls,\u8221\'94 he said forcefully. He pushed his empty bowl away. He\u8217\'92d been talking all this while and he\u8217\'92d already finished the porridge as well as a small plate of peppered leech. The man had a prodigious talent for eating and talking at the same time, as though the fat pink lip wiggling inside his beard was a baited hook, and the leeches were leaping at it. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93The true artist,\u8221\'94 Vigram said as he reached over Mandri\u8217\'92s plate to grab leech-paste pastry, \u8220\'93the true artist is a divine instrument. They must be kept apart from the self-skinny horde.\u8221\'94 He stuffed the pastry in his mouth, and now he talked out the side of his mouth in a muffled drawl. \u8220\'93There used to be word in Old Jandri which meant \u8216\'91artist\u8217\'92, but that word is lost to time.\u8221\'94 He took a heavy drink from his cup. \u8220\'93There is only: \u8216\'91bursheg\u8217\'92. It means something like \u8216\'91fertile ground\u8217\'92, but in the Solitant tradition it means \u8216\'91true artist\u8217\'92.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Interesting,\u8221\'94 Mandri lied.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll tell you what\u8217\'92s interesting,\u8221\'94 Vigram said, lifting his thick brows. \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ve heard it said that art has nothing to do with what a person makes. Have you ever heard that? I didn\u8217\'92t understand it at first, but you know, it\u8217\'92s true. True artistry, consider this\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 true artistry is a state of mind. Some of the greatest artists never made anything at all.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri stuffed his own mouth with a breadroll in a futile attempt to stifle himself. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I was under the impression,\u8221\'94 he said as he worked the roll into his cheek, \u8220\'93that an artist makes art. I mean, that seems like the most straightforward definition to me. I mean, if we\u8217\'92re getting upset about people twisting words, then\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram frowned and tutted, then robbed Mandri of the small slice of pie he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d been meaning to get to. \u8220\'93Nobody makes anything,\u8221\'94 he insisted. \u8220\'93We can only ever rearrange. When you paint, you push pigment around. How is that any different than my footprints rearranging sand? No, either everyone is an artist, or, and this is my claim, an artist is a certain type}{\f1\fs24\b0\i1  }{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 of}{\f1\fs24\b0\i1  }{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 person. A certain type of }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 mind}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 . You know, too many big ideas, too many shallow excuses, that sort of thing. It\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s a mind marked by excess\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 not abundance\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 excess}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 . The true artist is the ultimate expression of, well\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8230\'85\u8221\'94 Vigram\u8217\'92s voice trailed off, but he finished the thought by giving Mandri a smug, teasing look.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri swallowed hard and said, \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Are you asking me if I know?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram smiled. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93So exaggerated is the artist\u8217\'92s sense of self that it becomes impossible to describe them without resorting to sarcasm.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re referring to me?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s smile swerved. \u8220\'93There is no one else here.\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Two slaves stood at attention by the kitchen\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s double-swing doors. Vigram\u8217\'92s blindness to their existence was cruel, but this did not dismantle his point. Mandri did think highly of himself.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Why shouldn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t he?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 When he was ten, he could paint a portrait in oils that rivaled the old Jeketian masters. These weren\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t polish-jobs where the paint was thin and every hair was rendered into being like he\u8217\'92d lost the plot of reality. By his hand, a single stroke of umber was enough to define the chestnut skin, the high-arched cheek, the skull underneath, the light, the shadow, even the mood of the piece. Warms and cools in one single stroke! With twenty-four, he could find a vivid likeness. There might be a few extra nibbles to make a beauty\u8217\'92s eyes glisten and her cleavage heave, but nobody counted those. Well, rich men like Vigram counted them. Lascivious men counted them. Probably, every man counted them. Some women, presumably.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 And like any prideful artist, Mandri would strut around the grand Hrkan galleries and make clear his contempt for his contemporaries. He\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d stand in front of a painting and say, \u8220\'93This piece really }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 moves}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  me,\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94 and he\u8217\'92d make a show of walking away. All must bear witness to his mop of black hair as it flounced itself in time with his skinny, stiff-backed step. Or he\u8217\'92d say, \u8220\'93I weep at every stroke,\u8221\'94 and he\u8217\'92d flash a knowing smile. Back in those days, he\u8217\'92d say these things directly to a fellow artist\u8217\'92s face if he could get to it. He never thought of it as bullying because artists, like himself, were safe targets for playful derision; it wasn\u8217\'92t the person he was making fun of, it was their failed attempts to express themselves, and those were }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 completely}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  different things. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d never go after the person.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 No, never.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Artists were the best people. They needed tough skin, unearned confidence, and a flair for the dramatic. Without any of that, they die in obscurity. Then there is the servility. Above all, an artist must be servile to the hand that feeds. And look at that, Vigram had a lot of food at his table. And here he was, eating it.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri sighed. He\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d become the one thing he\u8217\'92d swore he\u8217\'92d never be: an employee.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Here he was, subjecting himself to a man who he did not know, }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 filtering}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  himself so as to not offend. Vigram was babbling on about artistry in the \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8216\'91classical sense\u8217\'92, as could only be found in the \u8216\'91uncorrupted ages\u8217\'92, and he was sitting here, taking it. Truer subjection could never be found.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 It wasn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t right.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d always said what he\u8217\'92d thought, and damn the consequences.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Why was he forgetting himself now? Because he desperately needed the money?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 No more.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Vigram,\u8221\'94 he said confidently, \u8220\'93you are an idiot.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram choked on a wad of smushed leech. He coughed, pounded his chest, then coughed again. Once recovered, he glared at Mandri with his protuberant eyes, oblivious to the brown specks of food in his long beard. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93In whose house do we sit?!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yours.\u8221\'94 Mandri said as he mustered a disarming smile. \u8220\'93But when it comes to these things, when it comes to matters of art, I am correct. If I am not correct, then you certainly aren\u8217\'92t.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why? Because I like some painters who aren\u8217\'92t you?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I don\u8217\'92t care who you like. And I don\u8217\'92t care what you think about art, or painting.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93If you don\u8217\'92t care, then why am I paying you for a lesson? Is it simply the money?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93No, this lesson is a charity.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93But I am going to }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 pay}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  you!\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Even so.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Leech juice dripped down the corner of Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s lip, accenting his frown. He wiped it away, then broke into a jolly smile. \u8220\'93Hah!\u8221\'94 he chortled as he stabbed a clam shell into a bowl of fermented leech. So much lard was mushed into those leeches that the gray paste could grease a wheel. Vigram\u8217\'92s outstretched tongue batted at the stringy slop before he slumped it all down his gullet. He patted his fat lips dry with his fifth napkin, then threw it onto the floor to join the others.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93We both know,\u8221\'94 he said, \u8220\'93that you degenerate artists only come here for the money.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Then we are both mistaken.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram rolled his eyes and set his leech lard mush aside. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Listen,\u8221\'94 he said. He put on his business face. \u8220\'93I should say that I am aware of your history.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93My history?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yes. You\u8217\'92ve given up on your talent. All you\u8217\'92ve done in the past year was rough up some backwater temple icon. I\u8217\'92ve also heard that you bought a farm nearby and it failed. Life is not going well, is it?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I can\u8217\'92t complain.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I want to know why you\u8217\'92ve given up on the craft. Did something untoward happen? Were you cheated?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93No, nothing like that,\u8221\'94 Mandri said. He fumbled around for something to say, because he would never explain this aspect of himself to anyone. \u8220\'93I suppose,\u8221\'94 he said, \u8220\'93I didn\u8217\'92t want to debase myself by doing what it takes to succeed.\u8221\'94}{\f1\fs24\b0\i1  }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Debase yourself!?\u8221\'94 Vigram chortled. \u8220\'93What a thing to say! Unless you mean, of course, that you refuse to partake in this world\u8217\'92s degeneracy, but even then, who cares about debasement? We\u8217\'92re already at the bottom. Success is success, by whatever means. Look at me\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 I should tell you how I got my start: I murdered my own father to inherit four ounces of silver.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s ears perked up. He studied Vigram closely, tried to find a sarcastic smile hiding in Vigram\u8217\'92s beard, but it was not there.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93That was only the first debasement,\u8221\'94 Vigram said plainly. \u8220\'93The second was to loan those four ounces out to a leech farm. You may wonder, why a leech farm? Beyond the blunt symbolism of the leech, there wasn\u8217\'92t much of a reason. I should say there }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 was}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  some logic to it\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 this particular farm supplied a Solitant temple with leeches for their bloodletting rituals. I took it to be a low risk investment, because temples are always the last thing the mob will torch in lean times. I waited for the lean times, when the bread was made from fern-roots\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 and that\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s when I squeezed. The farm\u8217\'92s owners asked for leniency on the interest rate, but I didn\u8217\'92t budge. I squeezed.\u8221\'94 Vigram held a slippery leech in his hand squeezed it hard before throwing it back in its bowl. \u8220\'93That\u8217\'92s how I took this farm,\u8221\'94 he said. \u8220\'93The leechmen accused me of committing usury against Solraheen Himself, because in some small way I was, but Solraheen is dead and so what does it matter? I made bold with a priest and prayed about it around a jug of beer. I flashed him a slip of silver, and the bleary shine blinded him to all my iniquity.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m sorry,\u8221\'94 Mandri said frankly. \u8220\'93I genuinely do not care.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Hah!\u8221\'94 Vigram laughed, and his laugh was a direct stab that hurt to hear. \u8220\'93That\u8217\'92s good, that\u8217\'92s good. You\u8217\'92re getting comfortable. And so quickly? Most people clam up when they discover that I\u8217\'92m not a good person. I should say that I }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 am}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  a good person if we understand \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8216\'91good\u8217\'92 in the sacred sense, but I will freely admit that I\u8217\'92m not \u8216\'91good\u8217\'92 in the degenerate sense that people usually mean.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I see.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Oh, It gets worse. You see, with the farm in hand, I lent smaller amounts over shorter terms to farmers who needed emergency loans to pay their taxes after droughts or infestations. I split these debts up and sold them off in Meskalim\u8217\'92s bond market. There\u8217\'92s not much money in Meskalim itself, but it has a busy port; access to all the important markets. From there, it was a simple matter of reducing my eyes to tiny pinpricks, ridding myself of limbs, segmenting the body, and now that I\u8217\'92d transformed into a leech, I attached myself }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 firmly}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  to the continent\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s rump and drank my fill. Anyone who tried to shake me off before I\u8217\'92d finished become my slave. I picked out the salvageable fools for my own use. Now, I have a whole brood of little leeches pouring over lists of sums credited and debts owed. So long as I maintain a layer of abstraction between these creatures and the men who collect, it\u8217\'92s all self-sustaining. I have a comfortable life. Idle hours. Believe me when I tell you, the debasement was worth every effort.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram licked his }{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 plump fingers clean of sun-dried leech oil. This oil was a true delicacy, squeezed as it was from the salivary glands of leeches aged twenty years or more. Leeches that big are more devourers than bloodsuckers, so they\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92re much more expensive to feed.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Now,\u8221\'94 Vigram said. \u8220\'93}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 You know all about the making of a painting. That\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s why you\u8217\'92re here, to teach me. But we\u8217\'92re going to have to do something about that willfullness. Ordinarily, I wouldn\u8217\'92t tolerate it, but you are here, in your homespun robe and ratty shoes, desperate for money, and that makes you pliable. I should say, there\u8217\'92s always that chance that you are exactly what I\u8217\'92m looking for. I\u8217\'92m keeping an open mind, because if I knew what I was looking for, I would have found it already.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Again,\u8221\'94 Mandri said, \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m not here for the money.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Then why walk all this way?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Because.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93}{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 Because?}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I don\u8217\'92t need a reason to do whatever I do. I do it. I\u8217\'92m here. That\u8217\'92s all.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram jaw slackened. For the first time he seemed to deeply consider something Mandri said. Or perhaps he was only swallowing down a bout of acid reflux.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Are you saying you\u8217\'92re aimless?\u8221\'94 he asked.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93No,\u8221\'94 Mandri answered. \u8220\'93All I\u8217\'92m saying is that I\u8217\'92m here. And on that subject, you know who isn\u8217\'92t?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Who?\u8221\'94 Vigram replied, intrigued.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Your friend who prefers to introduce herself.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Ah,\u8221\'94 Vigram said, relaxing. \u8220\'93Yes...you\u8217\'92re right, we\u8217\'92ve waited long enough. All she does is watch, anyways.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram clapped his meaty hands, prompting one of the nameless slaves to come and take his plates. Once done, he stood up. His chair protested the sudden shift of his massive weight with a terrible squeak.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93We will begin,\u8221\'94 he said.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri nodded, then wiped his own mouth and excused himself from the table. He took his time, because he wasn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t looking forward to beginning anything if Vigram was involved. But, he had to. He needed the money. He needed it quite badly. He just didn\u8217\'92t want to tell Vigram what it was for, or else the man might try to intervene.}}